    "body": "## What Changed\n\nTreat stored alias names as own JSON entries when resolving, creating, deleting, renaming, or updating aliases. Define new entries explicitly so a valid `__proto__` name is serialized as an ordinary property.\n\nExisting JSON-owned `__proto__`, `constructor`, `toString`, and `hasOwnProperty` records remain readable and writable. The public snapshot shape, accepted-name rules, transaction lock, and atomic publication behavior stay the same.\n\n## Why This Change\n\nThese names pass the existing alias-name validation, but the alias dictionary inherits properties from `Object.prototype`.\n\n- An absent inherited name resolves to a non-null session record with an undefined path.\n- Creating `__proto__` reports success but loses the record when the dictionary is serialized.\n- Other inherited names are incorrectly reported as existing, and renaming an ordinary alias to one is rejected.\n- Deleting, renaming, or changing the title of a missing inherited name can report success or mutate the inherited object.\n\nAll of these failures come from the same dictionary-key handling issue.\n\n## Testing Done\n\n- Exact-base regressions: **2 passed / 15 failed**. Candidate: **17 passed / 0 failed**.\n- The same before/after regression passes on Linux with Node 18, 20 and 22, Windows with Node 22, and macOS with Node 22.\n- Full `npm test` on clean Ubuntu / Node 22: **490/490 test files pass**, with complete execution integrity.\n- All four alias suites pass, including existing concurrent-writer, sharing-retry, and legacy JSON cases.\n- Changed-file ESLint passes. Changed-source coverage: **97.37% lines/statements, 97.24% branches, 100% functions**.\n- The new tests use an isolated `ECC_AGENT_DATA_HOME`, assert the exact fixture path, and restore any built-in properties that the old implementation mutates while demonstrating its failures.\n- [Exact-base/candidate platform regressions and full suite](https://github.com/Afloat16/ECC/actions/runs/43976024993), candidate `b504f3cd` against base `8abdf329`.\n\n- [ ] Manual testing completed\n- [ ] Automated full suite passes locally (`node tests/run-all.js`)\n- [x] Edge cases considered and tested\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] `fix:` Bug fix\n\n## Security & Quality Checklist\n\n- [x] No secrets or API keys committed\n- [x] No sensitive data exposed in regression fixtures\n- [x] Follows conventional commits format\n- [x] Independent code and regression-test review completed\n\nThe two-file patch has no dependency, package manifest, shell-script, or published-path changes.\n",
